{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-20459" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040213/state.json" "file_sha256" "44e2ac4aacf233f7f2832d58c9693faa75f215fbfd742d362808537a18d78975"} {"question" "q-20459" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & \\frac{10}{3} \\\\ 2 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & \\frac{10}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-2y=\\frac{10}{3} \\\\  & y=-\\frac{5}{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-\\frac{5}{3}$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-2(-\\frac{5}{3})=\\frac{10}{3}\\,⇒\\,x=\\frac{10}{3}-\\frac{10}{3}=0.\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=0$ and $y=-\\frac{5}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040213/state.json" "file_sha256" "44e2ac4aacf233f7f2832d58c9693faa75f215fbfd742d362808537a18d78975"} {"question" "q-20459" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040213/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dd27bde0e4244fdaa6cbf12d593d53d62