1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "reviewed_ma_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040213/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "62be2d9ad2a4716e7d82d90bf6acc0e7f58e570be8def3edeb91ba144c5e261d" "rationale" "Divide R1 by 2 to obtain [1,7/2,-5/2]. Subtract 7R1 from R2 to obtain [0,-27/2,27/2], then multiply R2 by -2/27 to obtain [0,1,-1]. Original option 4 matches. Stored bmatrix notation has identical matrix entries; the unresolved unsupported-escape result is not a mathematical contradiction. This is a source-backed derived judgment corroborated by the worked solution and successful grading."}] "usage" {"q-20496" [] "e-4698" [] "q-10522" [] "e-4697" []} "basis" 1420 "retractions" [[17592186059895 :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n${x - 3y =-8; 2x + 4y = 4$.\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system."] [17592186059895 :question/answer-fields 17592186056090] [17592186060126 :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n${2x + 7y =-5; 7x + 11y =-4$.\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form."] [17592186060126 :question/answer-fields 17592186057577] [17592186059508 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -8\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix."] [17592186059508 :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nM\\begin{vmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -8\\end{bmatrix} & R_{2}\\end{vmatrix}:=R_{2} + (-3)R_{1}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -8\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{2} \\mid:=-\\frac{1}{8}R_{2}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\nx + 2y = 0; y = 1\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=1$ tells us the value of $y$. Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+2(1)=0 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x=-2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=1$. Or, in vector form,\n\n$$\n\\left< -2,1 \\right>\n$$"] [17592186059509 :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n$-x + 5y = 5; x - 6y = 5$.\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system."] [17592186059509 :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nM\\begin{vmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{bmatrix} & R_{1}\\end{vmatrix}:=-R_{1}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}R_{2} &:=R_{2} + (-1)R_{1} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 10\\end{bmatrix} & R_{2}\\end{vmatrix}:=-R_{2}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\nx - 5y =-5; y =-10\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-10$ tells us the value of $y$. Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-5(-10)=-5 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x=-55\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-55$ and $y=-10$. Or, in vector form, $\\langle -55,-10 \\rangle$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186056091 17592186056092 17592186056093 17592186056094 17592186056095 17592186057578 17592186057579 17592186057580 17592186057581 17592186057582] "immutable_fields" [[17592186056090 :answer-field/correct] [17592186056090 :answer-field/id] [17592186056090 :answer-field/key] [17592186056090 :answer-field/type] [17592186057577 :answer-field/correct] [17592186057577 :answer-field/id] [17592186057577 :answer-field/key